# Blink block-flow layout — blink.layout.block_flow
#
# A minimal Block Formatting Context (BFC): boxes stack vertically inside their
# parent's content box, offset by the parent's border + padding and by each
# child's own margins.
#
# FLOATS, CLEAR AND MARGIN COLLAPSING (added 2026-08-11)
#
# These were blocker 7 of doc/03_plan/ui/rendering/blink_wiring_plan.md. The
# RULES are not implemented here — they live in `common/layout/float_bands.spl`
# and `common/layout/margin_collapse.spl`, which both blink and the live
# browser lane may import. blink is a LEAF (it imports only `blink`, `skia`,
# `common`) so it cannot reach the live lane's `layout_float.spl`, and copying
# that file in would have grown the very duplicate family the wiring plan
# exists to shrink. This module is only the blink-shaped DRIVER: it walks the
# arena, asks those modules where things go, and writes `SkRect`s.
#
# Participation is declared per box, on `BlockFlowBox` rather than on
# `BoxGeometry`: `float_side`, `clear`, and `establishes_bfc` are flow
# behaviour, not dimensions, and keeping `BoxGeometry` at three fields means
# every existing caller of it still compiles.
#
# THE INTERACTIONS, AND WHICH ARE HANDLED
#
# Handled:
#   - Adjacent in-flow siblings collapse their facing margins.
#   - A first in-flow child's margin-top collapses INTO its parent's own
#     margin-top (so the parent moves, not just the child), and a last in-flow
#     child's margin-bottom likewise, each only when no border, no padding, and
#     no BFC root separates them. This is computed by `effective_margin_top` /
#     `effective_margin_bottom`, which recurse down the first/last in-flow
#     child chain, so a collapse through several empty-edged wrappers is
#     modelled.
#   - Floats do NOT collapse margins with anything (CSS 2.1 §8.3.1) and are
#     skipped by the collapsing pass entirely.
#   - A float BETWEEN two in-flow siblings suppresses their collapse, because
#     their margins are no longer adjoining.
#   - `clear` moves a box down past the relevant floats, and a box that
#     actually gained clearance does NOT collapse its top margin with anything.
#   - In-flow boxes are narrowed and shifted by the floats beside them, over
#     the box's whole height band rather than at a single scanline.
#   - A box's auto height grows to contain its own floats.
#
# NOT handled — stated so the geometry is never silently wrong:
#   - Floats do not escape their parent. Each box gets its OWN float area, i.e.
#     every box behaves as a block formatting context root for float
#     containment. That is correct when the parent really is a BFC root and
#     wrong when it is not (a float should then overflow into the grandparent's
#     band). `establishes_bfc` therefore affects MARGIN collapsing only.
#   - Self-collapsing boxes: an empty box with no border/padding/height does
#     not collapse its own top and bottom margins together.
#   - Floats need a declared container width. blink has no auto/percentage
#     width, so a container with `width == 0.0` gives a zero-wide float band
#     and every float lands at the left edge.
#   - No float shrink-to-fit: a float uses its declared width. `place` already
#     overflows a too-wide float at the container edge (CSS 2.1 §9.5.1 rule 3)
#     rather than shrinking it, which is the spec behaviour for a DECLARED
#     width; what is missing is the `width: auto` shrink-to-fit sizing that
#     would have chosen a narrower width in the first place. blink has no
#     auto/percentage width at all, so this is that gap, not a float gap.
#
# CLOSED 2026-08-11 — line boxes ARE now shortened by floats.
#   `layout/inline_text.spl:layout_inline_text_around` takes a `FloatArea` and
#   lays each line box at its own y, wrapped to the band available over that
#   line's own height range and started at that band's left edge, so text flows
#   around a float instead of overlapping it. A line whose band is fully closed
#   is skipped and the cursor drops a line, so text resumes BELOW the float.
#   This module does not yet CALL it: `BlockFlowBox` carries no text, so the
#   caller that owns the run (the paint/style bridge) is the one that hands the
#   box's `FloatArea` over. That the driver has no inline content of its own is
#   why the fix lands in inline layout, which is where CSS puts it.
#
# Scope (other deliberate non-goals — see doc/08_tracking/bug/
# render_lane_specs_import_nonexistent_modules_2026-08-08.md):
#   - NO percentage sizing, NO shrink-to-fit; width is always as given
#   - NO absolute/fixed positioning, NO writing-mode/RTL
#   - Auto-height is minimal (added 2026-08-10, see `compute_layout`): a box
#     with a 0.0 (undeclared/`auto`) height grows to fit the content height it
#     just stacked. This is the narrow case needed so a text box's height
#     shows up in its parent's own rect; it is not real CSS shrink-to-fit
#     (no min/max-height, no interaction with floats or intrinsic width).
# Consumers: blink/paint/paint_tree_walker.spl, blink/input/hit_test.spl
#
# NAMING — this type was called `BlockLayoutBox` until 2026-08-10, which collided
# with three unrelated box records: `common.layout.box_model.BlockLayoutBox`
# (recursive value tree, scalar x/y/w/h), `common.render_scene.box_types.
# BlockLayoutBox` (class, EdgeSizes-grouped BoxModel) and `browser_engine/
# layout_box.spl.BeLayoutBox` (class, DOM-attached). They are genuinely
# different structures — this one is arena/id-based (`children_ids: [i64]`,
# `computed_rect: SkRect`) because the blink render-lane contract needs id
# lookup and skia rects, which `common/` (a no-skia-dependency tier) must not
# acquire. Renamed to `BlockFlowBox` so the four cannot be conflated.
#
# SPACING IS SHARED (merged 2026-08-10): `BoxGeometry` no longer declares its
# own twelve spacing edges. It nests `common.layout.box_model.BoxModel`, which
# was field-for-field identical, as `spacing`. Reach edges through it
# (`geo.spacing.margin_top`). Do not reintroduce a parallel edge record — the
# whole point is that a change to BoxModel is now felt by this lane too. See
# doc/08_tracking/bug/three_layoutbox_variants_2026-08-10.md.
#
# `width`/`height` stay on BoxGeometry: BoxModel deliberately carries no
# dimensions (its own consumer, `common.layout.BlockLayoutBox`, holds w/h alongside
# it), so nesting adds the edges without importing a sizing policy.

use std.skia.entity.geometry.{SkRect}
use std.common.layout.box_model.{BoxModel}
use std.common.layout.float_bands.{
    FloatArea, FloatRect, FloatSide, ClearKind, float_area_new
}
use std.common.layout.margin_collapse.{
    collapse_margins, collapsed_gap, siblings_margins_collapse,
    top_margin_collapses_with_parent, bottom_margin_collapses_with_parent
}

struct BoxGeometry:
    """Box dimensions plus the shared CSS edge record, in device-independent pixels."""
    width: f64
    height: f64
    spacing: BoxModel

fn box_geometry_zero() -> BoxGeometry:
    """Return a geometry with every edge and dimension at zero."""
    BoxGeometry(width: 0.0, height: 0.0, spacing: BoxModel.zero())

fn box_geometry_new(width: f64, height: f64, margin: f64, padding: f64, border: f64) -> BoxGeometry:
    """Return a geometry with uniform margin, padding and border on all four sides."""
    BoxGeometry(
        width: width,
        height: height,
        spacing: BoxModel(
            margin_top: margin, margin_right: margin,
            margin_bottom: margin, margin_left: margin,
            padding_top: padding, padding_right: padding,
            padding_bottom: padding, padding_left: padding,
            border_top: border, border_right: border,
            border_bottom: border, border_left: border
        )
    )

class BlockFlowBox:
    """One participant in the block flow: its geometry, flow role, children,
    and laid-out rect.

    `float_side` of `NoFloat` means the box is in normal flow. `clear` says
    which floats it must clear before being placed. `establishes_bfc` fences
    margin collapsing at this box's boundary (see the header for what it does
    NOT do)."""
    id: i64
    geometry: BoxGeometry
    float_side: FloatSide
    clear: ClearKind
    establishes_bfc: bool
    children_ids: [i64]
    computed_rect: SkRect

fn block_flow_box_new(id: i64, geometry: BoxGeometry) -> BlockFlowBox:
    """Create an unlaid-out in-flow box with no children and an empty rect."""
    BlockFlowBox(
        id: id,
        geometry: geometry,
        float_side: FloatSide.NoFloat,
        clear: ClearKind.NoClear,
        establishes_bfc: false,
        children_ids: [],
        computed_rect: SkRect(left: 0.0, top: 0.0, right: 0.0, bottom: 0.0)
    )

fn block_flow_box_floated(id: i64, geometry: BoxGeometry, side: FloatSide) -> BlockFlowBox:
    """Create an unlaid-out FLOATED box.

    A float is always a block formatting context root (CSS 2.1 §9.4.1), so
    `establishes_bfc` is set here rather than left to the caller to remember."""
    BlockFlowBox(
        id: id,
        geometry: geometry,
        float_side: side,
        clear: ClearKind.NoClear,
        establishes_bfc: true,
        children_ids: [],
        computed_rect: SkRect(left: 0.0, top: 0.0, right: 0.0, bottom: 0.0)
    )

fn block_flow_box_clearing(id: i64, geometry: BoxGeometry, clear: ClearKind) -> BlockFlowBox:
    """Create an unlaid-out in-flow box that clears floats on the given sides."""
    BlockFlowBox(
        id: id,
        geometry: geometry,
        float_side: FloatSide.NoFloat,
        clear: clear,
        establishes_bfc: false,
        children_ids: [],
        computed_rect: SkRect(left: 0.0, top: 0.0, right: 0.0, bottom: 0.0)
    )

fn block_flow_box_bfc_root(id: i64, geometry: BoxGeometry) -> BlockFlowBox:
    """Create an unlaid-out in-flow box that establishes a new BFC, so its
    margins never collapse with its children's."""
    BlockFlowBox(
        id: id,
        geometry: geometry,
        float_side: FloatSide.NoFloat,
        clear: ClearKind.NoClear,
        establishes_bfc: true,
        children_ids: [],
        computed_rect: SkRect(left: 0.0, top: 0.0, right: 0.0, bottom: 0.0)
    )

class LayoutContext:
    """An arena of layout boxes plus the viewport they are laid out in."""
    viewport_width: f64
    viewport_height: f64
    boxes: [BlockFlowBox]
    root_id: i64

fn layout_context_new(viewport_width: f64, viewport_height: f64) -> LayoutContext:
    """Create an empty layout context for the given viewport size."""
    LayoutContext(
        viewport_width: viewport_width,
        viewport_height: viewport_height,
        boxes: [],
        root_id: -1
    )

impl LayoutContext:
    fn add_box(box: BlockFlowBox):
        """Add a box to the arena. Ids are not checked for uniqueness."""
        self.boxes.push(box)

    fn set_root(id: i64):
        """Designate which box id compute_layout starts from."""
        self.root_id = id

    fn index_of(id: i64) -> i64:
        """Return the arena index of a box id, or -1 when absent."""
        var i = 0
        while i < self.boxes.len():
            if self.boxes[i as i32].id == id:
                return i
            i = i + 1
        -1

    fn get_box(id: i64) -> BlockFlowBox?:
        """Look up a box by id. Returns nil when no such box was added."""
        val idx = self.index_of(id)
        if idx < 0:
            return nil
        Some(self.boxes[idx as i32])

    fn first_in_flow_child(idx: i64) -> i64:
        """Arena index of the first non-floated child of `idx`, or -1.

        Floats are skipped because their margins never collapse with anything,
        so the first in-flow child is the one whose top margin can reach the
        parent's."""
        val kids = self.boxes[idx as i32].children_ids
        var i: i64 = 0
        while i < kids.len():
            val cidx = self.index_of(kids[i as i32])
            if cidx >= 0 and self.boxes[cidx as i32].float_side == FloatSide.NoFloat:
                return cidx
            i = i + 1
        -1

    fn last_in_flow_child(idx: i64) -> i64:
        """Arena index of the last non-floated child of `idx`, or -1."""
        val kids = self.boxes[idx as i32].children_ids
        var i: i64 = kids.len() - 1
        while i >= 0:
            val cidx = self.index_of(kids[i as i32])
            if cidx >= 0 and self.boxes[cidx as i32].float_side == FloatSide.NoFloat:
                return cidx
            i = i - 1
        -1

    fn effective_margin_top(idx: i64, depth: i64) -> f64:
        """The margin-top this box presents to its SIBLINGS and parent.

        When the box's own top edge does not separate it from its first in-flow
        child — no top border, no top padding, not a BFC root — that child's
        margin-top collapses INTO this one, and the pair present a single
        margin outward. The recursion walks the first-in-flow chain, so a
        margin can collapse up through several edgeless wrappers, which is what
        CSS 2.1 §8.3.1 describes. `depth` bounds the walk at 64 levels so a
        cyclic `children_ids` graph cannot hang layout."""
        val b = self.boxes[idx as i32]
        val own = b.geometry.spacing.margin_top
        if depth >= 64:
            return own
        if not top_margin_collapses_with_parent(
            b.geometry.spacing.border_top,
            b.geometry.spacing.padding_top,
            b.establishes_bfc,
            false
        ):
            return own
        val child = self.first_in_flow_child(idx)
        if child < 0:
            return own
        collapse_margins(own, self.effective_margin_top(child, depth + 1))

    fn effective_margin_bottom(idx: i64, depth: i64) -> f64:
        """The margin-bottom this box presents to its siblings and parent.

        Mirror of `effective_margin_top`. A DECLARED height (`height != 0.0` —
        this lane has no separate `auto` sentinel on `f64`) pins the parent's
        bottom content edge, so the last child's margin cannot reach out
        through it."""
        val b = self.boxes[idx as i32]
        val own = b.geometry.spacing.margin_bottom
        if depth >= 64:
            return own
        if not bottom_margin_collapses_with_parent(
            b.geometry.spacing.border_bottom,
            b.geometry.spacing.padding_bottom,
            b.geometry.height == 0.0,
            0.0,
            b.establishes_bfc
        ):
            return own
        val child = self.last_in_flow_child(idx)
        if child < 0:
            return own
        collapse_margins(own, self.effective_margin_bottom(child, depth + 1))

    fn compute_layout():
        """Lay out the tree from the root, stacking children vertically.

        No-op when no root was set or the root id is absent.
        """
        if self.root_id < 0:
            return
        val root_idx = self.index_of(self.root_id)
        if root_idx < 0:
            return

        # Recorded results, parallel arrays: laid_idx[k] gets rect laid_rect[k].
        var laid_idx: [i64] = []
        var laid_rect: [SkRect] = []
        # Work stack of (arena index, border-box left, border-box top).
        var stack: [(i64, f64, f64)] = []

        val root_geo = self.boxes[root_idx as i32].geometry
        val root_left = root_geo.spacing.margin_left
        # The root's own margin-top may have absorbed its first in-flow child's
        # (parent/child collapsing), so the outward margin is asked for rather
        # than read off the spacing record.
        val root_top = self.effective_margin_top(root_idx, 0)
        laid_idx.push(root_idx)
        laid_rect.push(SkRect(
            left: root_left,
            top: root_top,
            right: root_left + root_geo.width,
            bottom: root_top + root_geo.height
        ))
        stack.push((root_idx, root_left, root_top))

        while stack.len() > 0:
            val frame = stack.pop()
            val idx = frame.0
            val left = frame.1
            val top = frame.2
            val parent = self.boxes[idx as i32]
            val pg = parent.geometry
            val content_left = left + pg.spacing.border_left + pg.spacing.padding_left
            val content_top = top + pg.spacing.border_top + pg.spacing.padding_top
            # Right edge of the content box. `width` is the BORDER-box width
            # (the root rect is `left .. left + width`), so the far border and
            # padding come back off it. A zero width — this lane's `auto` —
            # leaves a zero-wide float band; that gap is stated in the header.
            val content_right = left + pg.width - pg.spacing.border_right - pg.spacing.padding_right

            # Floats placed by THIS box's children. One area per box: see the
            # header — floats do not escape their parent in this lane.
            val area = float_area_new()

            var cursor = content_top
            # Sibling-collapse state. `prev_margin_bottom` is the outward
            # margin of the previous in-flow sibling; `seen_in_flow` says
            # whether there was one; `float_since_last` records a float placed
            # between two in-flow siblings, which stops their margins adjoining.
            var prev_margin_bottom: f64 = 0.0
            var seen_in_flow = false
            var float_since_last = false

            for cid in parent.children_ids:
                val cidx = self.index_of(cid)
                if cidx >= 0:
                    val cbox = self.boxes[cidx as i32]
                    val cg = cbox.geometry
                    val ms = cg.spacing

                    if cbox.float_side != FloatSide.NoFloat:
                        # FLOATED CHILD. Its margins never collapse, so the
                        # margin box is simply the border box grown by them,
                        # and the cursor does NOT advance: a float is out of
                        # flow and the next in-flow sibling starts where this
                        # one would have.
                        val margin_w = cg.width + ms.margin_left + ms.margin_right
                        val margin_h = cg.height + ms.margin_top + ms.margin_bottom
                        val placed = area.place_and_add(
                            margin_w, margin_h, cbox.float_side,
                            cursor, content_left, content_right
                        )
                        val fleft = placed.left + ms.margin_left
                        val ftop = placed.top + ms.margin_top
                        laid_idx.push(cidx)
                        laid_rect.push(SkRect(
                            left: fleft,
                            top: ftop,
                            right: fleft + cg.width,
                            bottom: ftop + cg.height
                        ))
                        stack.push((cidx, fleft, ftop))
                        float_since_last = true
                    else:
                        # IN-FLOW CHILD. `clear` first: it decides where the
                        # box may start, and a box that actually moved has
                        # clearance, which suppresses its margin collapsing.
                        val cleared = area.clearance_for(cbox.clear, cursor)
                        val has_clearance = cleared > cursor
                        if has_clearance:
                            cursor = cleared

                        val child_mt = self.effective_margin_top(cidx, 0)
                        var gap: f64 = 0.0
                        if seen_in_flow:
                            if siblings_margins_collapse(false, cbox.establishes_bfc, has_clearance, float_since_last):
                                gap = collapsed_gap(prev_margin_bottom, child_mt)
                            else:
                                gap = prev_margin_bottom + child_mt
                        else:
                            # First in-flow child. When its margin collapsed
                            # OUT to the parent (already folded into the
                            # parent's own effective margin-top by
                            # `effective_margin_top`), adding it again here
                            # would double-count it, so the gap is zero.
                            if top_margin_collapses_with_parent(
                                pg.spacing.border_top, pg.spacing.padding_top,
                                parent.establishes_bfc, has_clearance
                            ):
                                gap = 0.0
                            else:
                                gap = child_mt

                        val ctop = cursor + gap
                        # Floats beside this box narrow AND shift it: its left
                        # edge is pushed past any left float overlapping the
                        # band it occupies.
                        var band_left = content_left
                        if not area.is_empty():
                            band_left = area.left_edge_at(ctop, cg.height, content_left)
                        val cleft = band_left + ms.margin_left
                        laid_idx.push(cidx)
                        laid_rect.push(SkRect(
                            left: cleft,
                            top: ctop,
                            right: cleft + cg.width,
                            bottom: ctop + cg.height
                        ))
                        stack.push((cidx, cleft, ctop))
                        cursor = ctop + cg.height
                        prev_margin_bottom = self.effective_margin_bottom(cidx, 0)
                        seen_in_flow = true
                        float_since_last = false

            # Close the last in-flow child's bottom margin. When it collapsed
            # OUT to the parent it is already in the parent's own effective
            # margin-bottom and must not also push the content box down.
            if seen_in_flow:
                if not bottom_margin_collapses_with_parent(
                    pg.spacing.border_bottom, pg.spacing.padding_bottom,
                    pg.height == 0.0, 0.0, parent.establishes_bfc
                ):
                    cursor = cursor + prev_margin_bottom

            # A box contains its own floats (CSS 2.1 §10.6.7): a float that
            # hangs below the last in-flow child still counts toward the
            # content height. This lane gives every box its own float area, so
            # this applies to every box, not only BFC roots.
            val floats_bottom = area.lowest_bottom()
            if floats_bottom > cursor:
                cursor = floats_bottom

            # Minimal auto-height (2026-08-10): a box with NO declared height
            # (`pg.height == 0.0`, CSS `auto`'s effective value in this lane,
            # since there is no separate "unset" sentinel on `f64`) grows to
            # fit the content it just stacked, rather than staying pinned to
            # 0. This is intentionally narrow — declared-nonzero heights are
            # left exactly as authored (still no shrink-to-fit, no
            # min/max-height) — but it is the minimum needed for a text box's
            # height to ever be visible in its parent's own rect, which is
            # the concrete gap this change closes. `cursor` has already
            # advanced past every child's margin-bottom, so
            # `cursor - content_top` is the stacked content height; add back
            # the padding/border the box still owes below that content.
            if pg.height == 0.0 and parent.children_ids.len() > 0:
                # `cursor - top` (NOT `cursor - content_top`) is the span from
                # the border-box top down to the end of the content, so it
                # already carries the top border and top padding. Measuring
                # from `content_top` dropped both — a box with 5px padding came
                # out 5px too short — fixed 2026-08-11 alongside floats.
                val auto_height = (cursor - top) + pg.spacing.padding_bottom + pg.spacing.border_bottom
                var k = 0
                while k < laid_idx.len():
                    if laid_idx[k as i32] == idx:
                        var r = laid_rect[k as i32]
                        r.bottom = r.top + auto_height
                        laid_rect[k as i32] = r
                    k = k + 1

        # Rebuild the arena with the computed rects (element write-back by value).
        var updated: [BlockFlowBox] = []
        var i = 0
        while i < self.boxes.len():
            val b = self.boxes[i as i32]
            var rect = b.computed_rect
            var k = 0
            while k < laid_idx.len():
                if laid_idx[k as i32] == i:
                    rect = laid_rect[k as i32]
                k = k + 1
            updated.push(BlockFlowBox(
                id: b.id,
                geometry: b.geometry,
                float_side: b.float_side,
                clear: b.clear,
                establishes_bfc: b.establishes_bfc,
                children_ids: b.children_ids,
                computed_rect: rect
            ))
            i = i + 1
        self.boxes = updated

    fn total_height_for(id: i64) -> f64:
        """Border-box height of a laid-out box; 0.0 when the id is absent."""
        val idx = self.index_of(id)
        if idx < 0:
            return 0.0
        val r = self.boxes[idx as i32].computed_rect
        r.bottom - r.top
